================================================================================
STEP 1: APPLY SUPABASE MIGRATIONS
================================================================================

The Supabase database schema must be created before the app can run.

Location: C:\Users\mcpag\lensello\apply-migrations.ps1

Instructions:

1. Open PowerShell
2. Run: .\apply-migrations.ps1
3. The script will:
   - Open the Supabase SQL editor in your browser
   - Copy each migration to your clipboard (one at a time)
   - Instruct you to paste into the SQL editor and run

4. Apply these 11 migrations in order:
   ✓ 20260813120000_client_portal.sql
   ✓ 20260813120100_print_sales.sql
   ✓ 20260813120200_campaign_planner.sql
   ✓ 20260813120300_conversations.sql
   ✓ 20260813120400_studio.sql
   ✓ 20260813120500_automations.sql
   ✓ 20260813120600_academy.sql
   ✓ 20260813130100_prints_followup.sql
   ✓ 20260813130200_planner_followup.sql
   ✓ 20260813130300_conversations_followup.sql
   ✓ 20260813130600_academy_followup.sql
   ✓ 20260813140000_drive_import.sql

What Each Migration Does:

Foundation Schemas (7 files):
- client_portal.sql: Gallery sections, portal sessions, display styles
- print_sales.sql: Products, orders, items, lab fulfillment
- campaign_planner.sql: Playbooks, tasks, campaign tasks
- conversations.sql: Threads, messages, contact identities
- studio.sql: Asset labels, requests, shortlist, generated images
- automations.sql: Automations, steps, runs, API keys
- academy.sql: Modules, lessons, worksheets, business profile

Follow-up Migrations (4 files):
- prints_followup.sql: Seed UK print catalogue (11 SKUs)
- planner_followup.sql: Seed 8 seasonal playbooks (66 tasks)
- conversations_followup.sql: Threading triggers and backfill
- academy_followup.sql: Academy content seeds

Drive Import (1 file):
- drive_import.sql: Drive import job and file tracking tables


================================================================================
STEP 2: CONFIGURE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
================================================================================

You need to gather credentials from your service providers and set them in
Vercel. Each service is independent — you can configure them one at a time.

Required Credentials:

GOOGLE WORKSPACE (Calendar + Drive)
├─ Service Account Email: <service-account@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com>
├─ Service Account Private Key: <-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----...>
└─ Calendar ID: <studio-calendar@google.com>

POSTMARK (Email)
├─ Server Token: <postmark-server-token>
└─ From Email: <studio@lensello.example>

STRIPE (Payments)
└─ Secret Key: <sk_live_...>

META (Social Publishing & Ads)
├─ App ID: <app-id>
├─ App Secret: <secret>
├─ Ad Account ID: <account-id>
└─ Ads Access Token: <token>


How to Set Environment Variables in Vercel:

Method 1: Via Web Dashboard
1. Go to vercel.com
2. Select project: lensello-web
3. Settings → Environment Variables
4. Add each variable with its value
5. Redeploy

Method 2: Via CLI (if you have Vercel CLI installed)
Run these commands:

vercel env add GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL
vercel env add GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY
vercel env add GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID
vercel env add POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN
vercel env add LENSELLO_FROM_EMAIL
vercel env add STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
vercel env add META_APP_ID
vercel env add META_APP_SECRET
vercel env add META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID
vercel env add META_ADS_ACCESS_TOKEN


