================================================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

Issue: App shows "Database connection failed"
Solution: Supabase migrations have not been applied. Run apply-migrations.ps1

Issue: Emails not sending
Solution: Set POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN and LENSELLO_FROM_EMAIL environment
variables in Vercel. Then redeploy.

Issue: Calendar events not syncing
Solution: Ensure GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL, GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY,
and GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID are set. Verify the service account has calendar access.

Issue: Payments failing
Solution: Verify STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is correct (sk_live_... not sk_test_...).
Check Stripe dashboard for configuration issues.

Issue: Social publishing not working
Solution: If not using Meta, the app falls back to mock mode. No errors should
appear. If errors appear, check META_APP_ID and META_APP_SECRET.


================================================================================
ARCHITECTURE NOTES
================================================================================

Technology Stack:
- Frontend: Next.js 16 with App Router (Server Components)
- Database: Supabase PostgreSQL with Row-Level Security
- Payments: Stripe API
- Email: Postmark API
- Calendar: Google Calendar API (service account)
- File Storage: Google Drive API (service account)
- Social: Meta API (Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, Pinterest)
- Deployment: Vercel

Key Architectural Decisions:

1. Service Accounts (not OAuth)
   - No consent screen required
   - Works for internal studio use
   - Shared credentials for Calendar and Drive

2. Lazy Integration Resolution
   - Each capability resolves on first use
   - Missing credentials throw on use, not on startup
   - One missing credential doesn't block others

3. Fail-Closed in Live Mode
   - Orders that report success without reaching the lab are worse than failures
   - Mock lab is used for demonstration only
   - Live mode throws visible errors for unconfigured services

4. Idempotent Migrations
   - Migrations can be re-run without duplicating data
   - Seeds use "ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING" patterns
   - Safe for CI/CD pipelines

5. Resume-Safe Photo Import
   - Photos tracked by job ID and file ID
   - No interim "importing" status that could strand on crash
   - Safe to interrupt and resume


